            "title": "Trump says 'representatives' will buy $200B in mortgage bonds",
            "description": "<p>President Trump said in a social media post on Thursday that he is \"instructing representatives\" to buy $200 billion in mortgage bonds, which he says will lower monthly payments and make home ownership more affordable.</p>\n<p>ResiClub co-founder and CEO Lance Lambert explains what this would mean for home buyers, telling Asking for a Trend host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> that it may not make a huge dent in the housing affordability crisis.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/asking-for-a-trend/\">Asking for a Trend</a>.</p>",
